    "title": "Bug Squasher: One star too few",
    "language": "html",
    "problemDescription": "Clicking the third star fills only two stars, and clicking the first one fills none. The loop stops one star early.",
    "buggyCode": "<div id=\"r\">\n  <i>o</i><i>o</i><i>o</i><i>o</i>\n</div>\n<script>\n  var items = document.querySelectorAll('#r i');\n  items.forEach(function (item, index) {\n    item.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      items.forEach(function (x, i) {\n        x.textContent = i < index ? '*' : 'o';\n      });\n    });\n  });\n</script>",
    "solution": {
      "code": "<div id=\"r\">\n  <i>o</i><i>o</i><i>o</i><i>o</i>\n</div>\n<script>\n  var items = document.querySelectorAll('#r i');\n  items.forEach(function (item, index) {\n    item.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      items.forEach(function (x, i) {\n        x.textContent = i <= index ? '*' : 'o';\n      });\n    });\n  });\n</script>",
      "explanation": "Positions start at 0, so the third star has index 2. Filling the stars with i < index leaves out the clicked one, and i <= index includes it."
    },
